ning: The deployments for frontend, geo, profile, rate, recommendation, reservation, search, and user are not in a ready state (READY: 0/1). To diagnose the root cause, I need to inspect the underlying pods for these deployments. The command "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation" will reveal if pods are crashing, pending, or in a failed state. This will help identify specific issues like image pull errors, configuration mismatches, or resource constraints.  \n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=473, prompt_tokens=3249, total_tokens=3722, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfac0-c40f-77f2-8dbe-dd28f2fa27f1-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3249, 'output_tokens': 473, 'total_tokens': 3722}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='67fe2c58-8b8e-4267-bf81-868004ee4ad7')]]
