ibe pod` output, the container is named `hotel-reserv-frontend`. We need to retrieve the current deployment YAML to confirm the exact container name and ensure the image update command uses the correct identifier.  \n\n```json\n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl get deployment frontend -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"\n  }\n}\n```', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=490, prompt_tokens=5554, total_tokens=6044, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfac2-c0db-78b2-94d3-df6add68e1fb-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5554, 'output_tokens': 490, 'total_tokens': 6044}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='89ed30c7-722b-4497-b388-e2fb167c1f2e')]]
