dy used kubectl get pods. Maybe they should check the pod's description again to confirm the image. Alternatively, check the logs again to see if the crash is due to a different reason now that the image is correct. \n\nThe user's last command was kubectl get pods, which shows the pod is still in CrashLoopBackOff. The next step is to check the logs or describe the pod again to see if the image is now correct. Since the image update was successful, the pod should pull the new image. If the pod is still crashing, the issue might be with the new image or another configuration problem. \n\nSo, the best next step is to describe the pod again to check the current status and events, ensuring the correct image is being used. If the image is correct, then the problem might be with the application inside the container, such as missing dependencies or configuration errors. Alternatively, check the logs for any new errors after the image update.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod frontend-78986558db-2txmx -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b20475d466c64441', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 600, 'prompt_tokens': 8236, 'total_tokens': 8836, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfac3-311c-7c60-aed0-31e106a6b763-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod frontend-78986558db-2txmx -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b20475d466c64441', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8236, 'output_tokens': 600, 'total_tokens': 8836}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl comm