ds -n hotel-reservation"\n  }\n}\n```', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 369, 'prompt_tokens': 7354, 'total_tokens': 7723, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfac3-5187-7c52-b56e-84ebf1749f45-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7354, 'output_tokens': 369, 'total_tokens': 7723}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5dd6fd19-0e37-44e0-963b-8b8cb21d41f9'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to fix an issue with the frontend service in their Kubernetes cluster. The problem started when the frontend pod was crashing because the container image was incorrect. They tried updating the deployment\'s image reference, but there were some issues with the container name and the image pull.\n\nFirst, they checked the deployment YAML and saw that the container name was "hotel-reserv-frontend" instead of "frontend". That\'s why the initial command to update the image failed. After correcting the container name in the kubectl set image command, the image update was successful. However, the pod was still in a CrashLoopBackOff state, which means it wasn\'t running properly.\n\nThe user then tried to describe the old pod, but it wasn\'t found, indicating that a new pod had been created. They needed to check the current pods to see if the new one was running. When they listed the pods, they saw that the frontend pod was now in a Running state. This suggests that the image update worked, and the new pod is using the correct image.\n\nBut to be thorough, they should check the logs of the new pod to ensure there are no other issues. If the pod is running without errors, the problem is resolved. If there are still issues, they might need to look into other factors like configuration errors or dependencies. However, based on the current information, the image was the main issue, and updating it fixed the problem.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ddf085230cc64cf', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 340, 'prompt_tokens': 8506, 'total_tokens': 8846, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfac3-636e-7a73-bea3-67857d2b6029-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ddf085230cc64cf', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8506, 'output_tokens': 340, 'total_tokens': 8846}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                      READY   STATUS             RESTARTS      AGE\nconsul-5c696cc4dc-ptjzq                   1/1     Running            0             6m15s\nfrontend-6df8475df4-pljkq                 1/1     Running            0             22s\ngeo-7bf795c745-q2hcn                      0/1     CrashLoopBackOff   4 (93s ago)   3m37s\njaeger-5b9775bd94-s4vvz                   1/1     Running            0             6m11s\nmemcached-profile-6849578b8-7h4c2         1/1     Running            0             6m8s\nmemcached-rate-948594dfd-v4lp5            1/1     Running            0             6m3s\nmemcached-reserve-68dbb57476-nw9d7        1/1     Running            0             5m51s\nmongodb-geo-8cb7d9f5b-cfgt7               1/1    